  "$comment": "X5.3 / DEC-M5-2: the RRR geometry of ArmDynamics3R built from the M3 spatial stdlib. Base body (1 kg at the pivot, yaw inertia Jb = 0.05) on a compliant Revolute3D about world z; upper arm and forearm joints about world -y (joint frame Rx(90 deg), local z = -y); point masses m2 = 2 at the elbow and m3 = 1 at the tip as RigidBody3D with 1e-8 kg m^2 principal moments, links l2 = 0.4 and l3 = 0.3 as FixedTransform3DNeutral. The torque sources, controller and TimeTable references are those of model rrr-torque. Held directions have kt = kr = 1e+08, and the arm is released on its static deflections; the only difference to the equation block is the joint compliance (and the 1e-8 point-mass inertias).",
